<%#
  reCAPTCHA widget.

  Expects `captcha` = { siteKey, mode, version }. Renders nothing when no site
  key is configured, so a form never shows a broken widget.

  Three shapes, and the version has to match the key or nothing works at all:

    v2 checkbox  - the familiar "I'm not a robot" box. Works with a standard v2 key.
    v2 invisible - no box. The challenge appears only when Google is unsure, so a
                   normal visitor sees nothing. Needs a key registered as
                   "reCAPTCHA v2 - Invisible"; a checkbox key also works here,
                   because Google ignores the request and draws the box anyway.
    v3           - no widget and no challenge ever. Google scores the visit in
                   the background and the server decides from the score. Needs a
                   v3 key; a v2 key cannot answer a v3 request.

  No data-callback here. The v2 widget is rendered explicitly by main.js, which
  passes the callback in the render options - a callback named in the markup
  would have to be a global, and it could not tell one form's widget from
  another's on a page that carries two.

  v3 has nothing to render. It just needs somewhere to put the token, which
  main.js fills in on submit. The hidden field carries the site key so the
  script can find it without a second lookup.
%>
<% if (captcha && captcha.siteKey) { %>
  <% if (captcha.version === 'v3') { %>
    <div class="recaptcha-wrap recaptcha-v3">
      <input type="hidden" name="g-recaptcha-response" value=""
             data-recaptcha-v3="<%= captcha.siteKey %>">
      <p class="form-hint" style="text-align:center">
        Protected by reCAPTCHA. No action needed — verification is automatic.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% } else if (captcha.mode === 'invisible') { %>
    <div class="recaptcha-wrap">
      <div class="g-recaptcha"
           data-sitekey="<%= captcha.siteKey %>"
           data-size="invisible"
           data-badge="bottomright"></div>
      <p class="form-hint" style="text-align:center">
        Protected by reCAPTCHA. No action needed — verification is automatic.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% } else { %>
    <div class="recaptcha-wrap">
      <div class="g-recaptcha" data-sitekey="<%= captcha.siteKey %>"></div>
    </div>
  <% } %>
<% } %>
